  '**The third, which is the one I kept.** _"A third consideration, which is rarely raised, is that the person who drafts a notice is the last person who can tell whether it is readable. I have drafted paragraphs of that kind for nineteen years. Four clerks in my own office asked me in a fortnight what one of them meant, and I had written it."_',
