  '_The point in both: a hedge made of evidence cannot be taken out by a sub-editor._',
  '**The old paragraph, with three examples.** _"There are many instances of this in the copy I receive. Contributors frequently hedge claims they could have supported. It is widely accepted that vague writing is a problem in trade publishing. In addition, several of my colleagues have made the same observation. Clearly this is an issue worth addressing."_ Fifty-one words, four sentences, and not one figure that anybody could check.',
