out.push(NOTE('The last paragraph of this model teaches something that appears nowhere else in the book and is worth naming for the class: **knowing which conclusion you have earned is part of the skill, and so is knowing which one your position allows.** The fourth conclusion is the strongest of the four by every measure the unit has taught, and Lubna is right not to use it. ⚠ In the **exam**, that second judgement does not apply — there is no one to offend and the strongest earned conclusion is the one to write. Say so explicitly, or the more thoughtful students in the class will hold back in the paper for reasons that are correct at work and costly in an examination. The distinction is between what is earned and what is affordable, and only the first of the two is marked.'));
