out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The four checks for the last four minutes are the most practical thing in Unit 3 and they are in a fixed order: both notes present · a concession with a limit · one example and not three · the first and last sentences read together.** Nothing else. Not spelling, not vocabulary, not making it nicer. And the repair rule matters as much as the checks: **make the smallest repair that fixes it, and never rewrite a paragraph in the last four minutes** — a missing note is one clause, a missing concession is one sentence in front of paragraph two, and an unfinished repair costs more than the fault did. Note also the finding that no class predicts: the commonest fault the reading-back turns up is **the missing example inside the conceded paragraph**, because a concession feels like a courtesy and so gets no evidence.'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
