out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready – Unit 3 quiz'));
out.push(A('**1** _Time, rather than patience, **is** what explaining costs_ — the subject is _time_; the plural noun in the middle pulls the verb.   **2** _which is **rarely** raised_ — adverb, not adjective.   **3** _**Take** the case of the four sites_ — _make the case_ exists and means something else.   **4** _enough to **show** that_ — bare infinitive after _enough to_.   **5** _not whether the rule is right, **but** whether anybody has read it_ — the contrast needs _but_.   **6** _His **concession** that the figure was wrong_ — the noun, from the declared word-formation set.'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** Open — the four descriptors are read in the class\'s own words before the recording, and not discussed yet.'));
out.push(A('**b** The hardest is **descriptor two**, communicative achievement — and the question that makes it countable is _does the writer hold the same position in paragraph four as in paragraph one, and did they get there by weighing rather than by repeating?_ And what happens when they read their own 1.7 essays is that **every one of them has something in it that four weeks of teaching did not put there**.'));
out.push(A('**c** Open; listen and read together.'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **Descriptor four is the most counter-intuitive fact about the paper and the class will not believe it without being shown: _range_ comes before _accuracy_.** Eleven correct simple sentences score **below** eight sentences of three shapes with two errors in them. That is _range not demonstrated_ from Unit 1 — Hiba\'s three words — arriving in a mark scheme four weeks later, and the connection should be drawn out loud. The practical consequence for marking a classmate is in the Language box and it is easy to skip: **count the shapes before you count the errors.** A student who marks errors first will rank Essay A above Essay B every time, and Essay B is the essay that will improve.'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('No Practise line in x.7: the Language box here sorts rather than drills, and the sorting is done in Stage 3 on two essays the class has not seen.'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Essay A)'));
